From: Techniix
Subject: [PATCH] util: link libgnu for inotify on Renga

fossilize_db.c uses inotify when meson.build finds sys/inotify.h. Renga
has that header and implements inotify in libgnu, not libroot, so
libEGL_mesa.so failed to link on Renga 143b8c30 with undefined
inotify_init1, inotify_add_watch and inotify_rm_watch. Link libgnu into
libmesa_util on Haiku/Renga when the header is present. The same change
is on Techniix/mesa renga-26.3 (32e1fb32) for NVK.

Generated-by: LLM
Biblioklept: this patch description was written by an AI model.
---
diff --git a/src/util/meson.build b/src/util/meson.build
index e1be8c5..728c87f 100644
--- a/src/util/meson.build
+++ b/src/util/meson.build
@@ -254,6 +254,12 @@ if with_platform_haiku
   deps_for_libmesa_util += dep_network
 endif
 
+# Renga provides inotify, which fossilize_db.c uses when sys/inotify.h is
+# found, in libgnu rather than libroot.
+if host_machine.system() == 'haiku' and cc.check_header('sys/inotify.h')
+  deps_for_libmesa_util += cc.find_library('gnu')
+endif
+
 if with_perfetto
   files_mesa_util += files(
     'perf/u_perfetto.cc',
